(658431, 67293, 13390, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by terje:</b></div><hr/><i> Thank you all for your comments! I''m very pleased with the results of this picture, although I agree with some of you that the text on the eggs is a bit distracting. I wanted to make sure you all knew it was eggs, here marking eggs is very common. <br/> <br/>To the ones who ask how it was done... it''s rather simple really: <br/>I glued a small blue thread to the cue ball, and for the first 0,5seconds the white ball was right infront of the eggs, then Marianne helped me pull the egg towards my cue. A total exposure for about 2 seconds. This was our 5th shot, and no eggs was harmed in this production. :-)<br/> <br/>Thanks again and good luck! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It would probably be a LOT more fun to actually shoot the eggs!</td>', 'Originally posted by terje: Thank you all for your comments! I''m very pleased with the results of this picture, although I agree with some of you that the text on the eggs is a bit distracting. I wanted to make sure you all knew it was eggs, here marking eggs is very common.  To the ones who ask how it was done... it''s rather simple really: I glued a small blue thread to the cue ball, and for the first 0,5seconds the white ball was right infront of the eggs, then Marianne helped me pull the egg towards my cue. A total exposure for about 2 seconds. This was our 5th shot, and no eggs was harmed in this production. :-) Thanks again and good luck!   It would probably be a LOT more fun to actually shoot the eggs!', '2004-04-07 21:38:45.000000', NULL, 0),
